<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kaiser</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kaiser is the German word for emperor, derived from the Roman name Caesar. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> it was the title of the King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-emperor">German Emperor</a>, first held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-i">Wilhelm I</a> from 1871. The Kaiser controlled foreign policy and the army and appointed the chancellor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kaiser.jpg" alt="Kaiser" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrayal_of_Franz_Joseph_and_his_wife_Elisabeth_on_a_millennium_memorial_leaf_with_the_crown.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
